{"name":"Gardener’s Soil","hex":"#5c534d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gardener","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who gardens; one who grows plants or cultivates a garden.","A coachman who drives badly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gardener"},{"term":"soil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mixture of mineral particles and organic material, used to support plant growth.","The unconsolidated mineral or organic material on the immediate surface of the earth that serves as a natural medium for the growth of land plants."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make dirty.","To become dirty or soiled."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soil","blocks":[{"text":"Soil, also commonly referred to as earth, is a mixture of organic matter, minerals, gases, water, and organisms that together support the life of plants and soil organisms. Some scientific definitions distinguish dirt from soil by restricting the former term specifically to displaced soil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Stagnogley.JPG/330px-Stagnogley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil","wikidata":"Q36133"},{"title":"Gardener","blocks":[{"text":"A gardener is someone who practices gardening, either professionally or as a hobby."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Abel_Grimmer_-_Spring_-_WGA10683.jpg/330px-Abel_Grimmer_-_Spring_-_WGA10683.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gardener","wikidata":"Q758780"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/500px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/